CONTROL name=staged-precondition-refusals-fire fired=RED honest log: admitted 17/17 tensors, 537215744 B of the artifact re-hashed against the log's own read-back digests. One field changed at a time: no RESULT line -> staged-evidence-result-line; the artifact renamed -> staged-evidence-artifact-name; one read-back digest flipped (all three on that line, so the equality inside the log still holds) -> staged-evidence-region-digest; that run's file_off shifted one byte -> staged-evidence-layout; only the read-back digest flipped while the log still calls it MATCH -> staged-evidence-readback; the TENSOR record for one policy-A tensor removed -> staged-evidence-incomplete; that tensor's type declared Q4_K against the artifact's Q8_0 -> staged-evidence-width. One refusal tag is deliberately unwitnessed: staged-evidence-artifact-size would require editing the pinned artifact, which no gate in this repo does. An admissions check that only ever says yes is the failure window-c found in M1
CONTROL name=topk-form-probe-distinguishes-the-wrong-form fired=RED limit=0 from the §10.6 exactness row (never typed here). The emitted cast-first weights reproduce the pinned bf16 record and the f32 weights reproduce the pinned f32 record on every arm (policy_a:cast-first=0,f32=0,ref_bf16:cast-first=0,f32=0); the arm-basis-leak form is refused with ndiff [4, 0], and on the arm whose routed_sum licence IS exactness (ref_bf16) the product built from f32-carry weights is refused by ndiff [1326] against the product built from cast-first weights [0]. If policy A ever computes R1 in the model dtype natively the leak form coincides with the emitted one and this control has nothing left to distinguish: it must be re-derived against new pinned material, not deleted
